    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:d1bf136a4a3c936a",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "e227336a5980961a1393e96ae8d9a364fc49cbe6bcdf30d03a05aa886ce9cb28",
      "text": "Early rise and transfer to the dock. Depart by motorized curiara boats up the Carrao River to Mayupa Lagoon and the Arautayma rapids. Short walk and breakfast at the camp with views of the stunning Auyan Tepui. Continue toward the Devil’s Canyon.\n\nArrive at Ratonsito Island, trek through virgin forest for about an hour to the viewpoint near the cliff edge, just meters from the world’s tallest waterfall – Angel Falls. Swim in the waterfall’s lagoon if desired. Return to the island for a traditional indigenous lunch.\n\nYou will also visit Pemon Indians, enjoy a musical performance, buy souvenirs, and taste local cuisine (ant sauce, Moriche palm caterpillars, cassava bread).\n\nMeals: light breakfast, lunch, dinner",
